# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Wired into the tsan build only, via gtest_discover_tests(... PROPERTIES
# ENVIRONMENT TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...) in tests/unit_tests/CMakeLists.txt.
#
# RULE: nothing in this file may name a symbol from our own code
# (market_data::, md_core, md_wire, aggregator, client). Our code is the
# signal TSan exists to give us. Every entry here is an uninstrumented
# third-party library whose internals TSan cannot see accurately, which
# DESIGN.md section 10 calls out explicitly for boost, gRPC and OpenSSL.

# gRPC ThreadManager tears down its worker-thread list during
# grpc::Server::Shutdown()/~Server(). TSan reports a read/write race on the
# std::list node count between two gRPC-internal threads swapping the list.
# gRPC is linked from vcpkg without instrumentation, so its own happens-before
# edges (the ThreadManager mutex) are invisible and this is a false positive.
# Seen on RoutingTest.* (5 tests), all of which stand up a real gRPC server.
race:grpc::ThreadManager

# The rest of gRPC (C++ layer, C core, and the posix EventEngine) plus the
# Abseil it is built on. All linked from vcpkg WITHOUT instrumentation, so
# their internal synchronisation is invisible to TSan: the EventEngine
# run-queue, Abseil's SpinLock / Waiter / status refcount, and the gpr
# allocators all establish happens-before that TSan cannot see, so any race
# confined to their frames is a false positive - the same basis as the
# ThreadManager entry above. These fire on RoutingTest.* once frames are
# symbolised (grpc 1.81's EventEngine spins up "event_engine" /
# "grpc_global_tim" threads that touch AnyInvocable closures and a
# flat_hash_map across threads).
race:grpc::
race:grpc_core::
race:grpc_event_engine::
race:gpr_
race:absl::

# libzmq is statically linked and uninstrumented. Its lock-free SPSC command
# and message pipes (ypipe_t / yqueue_t) hand objects from the application
# thread to the ZMQbg/IO background thread through atomics TSan cannot model,
# and msg_t init/close runs on the message handed across. TSan then reports
# the queued command_t / msg_t payload as raced with no happens-before edge.
# Seen on every ZmqProviderSink / ZmqCoreIngress test.
race:zmq::
